.TH "PKGSOURCE_PLAN_ADAPTER" "3" "" "libpkgsource\-plan 1.0.0" "libpkgsource\-plan"
.SH NAME
pkgsource_plan_adapter \- project sealed source authority into planner facts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include <libpkgsource\-plan/libpkgsource\-plan.h>

pkgsource::plan_adapter::candidate_projection
pkgsource::plan_adapter::project_candidate(
    pkgsource::source_snapshot source);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[CR]project_candidate()\f[R] consumes one complete sealed \f[CR]pkgsource::source_snapshot\f[R] and returns a \f[CR]pkgsource::plan_adapter::candidate_projection\f[R] containing both the original source authority and one \f[CR]pkgplan::candidate_package_fact\f[R] derived from it.
.PP
The planner fact contains:
.IP \[bu] 2
each normalized runtime package requirement as one planner runtime dependency;
.IP \[bu] 2
pre\-remove and post\-remove programs as exact removal\-lifecycle material with format \f[CR]text/x\-posix\-shell\f[R];
.IP \[bu] 2
the normalized target architecture set as the target\-profile fact \f[CR]pkgsource.target\-architectures\f[R];
.IP \[bu] 2
package name, version, distribution release, and the source\-issued package release identity.
.PP
An empty target architecture set is represented by \f[CR]*\f[R].
A constrained set is a comma\-separated sequence in the normalized order supplied by \f[CR]libpkgsource\f[R].
.PP
Build and check requirements, lifecycle requirements, selected profiles, build architecture constraints, source inputs, build and check programs, pre\-install and post\-install programs, source origin, and source\-snapshot identity do not become planner candidate control.
They remain available through the retained source snapshot.
.SH OWNERSHIP
The input snapshot is taken by value.
The returned \f[CR]pkgsource::plan_adapter::candidate_projection\f[R] owns that snapshot and the projected planner fact.
Passing an rvalue transfers the snapshot without an additional copy.
.PP
The adapter does not reopen source paths or mutate the snapshot.
.SH IDENTITIES
The source package\-release SHA\-256 bytes are imported into the corresponding planner release\-identity value without recomputation.
.PP
Candidate\-control identity is computed over the constructed, planner\-normalized runtime dependencies, removal lifecycle, and target\-profile facts using the domain \f[CR]libpkgsource\-plan/candidate\-control/v1\f[R].
Package release coordinates and source\-snapshot identity do not participate in candidate\-control identity.
.PP
The byte\-level contract and fixed vector are specified in \f[CR]CANDIDATE\-CONTROL\-IDENTITY\-1.md\f[R] in the source distribution.
.SH ERRORS
\f[CR]pkgsource::plan_adapter::projection_error\f[R] is thrown for adapter\-owned projection failures.
.TP
\f[CR]pkgsource::plan_adapter::projection_error_code::identity\f[R]
Identity framing, SHA\-256 processing, or source release\-identity decoding failed.
.TP
\f[CR]pkgsource::plan_adapter::projection_error_code::planner_fact\f[R]
A projected value raised \f[CR]pkgplan::fact_error\f[R] while constructing a \f[CR]libpkgplan\f[R] fact.
Other standard exceptions are not reclassified.
.SH AUTHORITY
The adapter translates only facts already owned by \f[CR]libpkgsource\f[R] and \f[CR]libpkgplan\f[R].
It does not parse source documents, resolve requirements, choose package candidates, construct transaction operations, execute programs, or store evidence.
.SH ABI
The public library is \f[CR]libpkgsource\-plan.so.1\f[R].
The public API depends on \f[CR]libpkgsource\f[R] 3.0 or later and \f[CR]libpkgplan\f[R] 0.2 or later.
Libcrypto is a private implementation dependency used for candidate\-control identity.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]libpkgsource(3)\f[R], \f[CR]pkgsource_snapshot(3)\f[R], \f[CR]libpkgplan(3)\f[R]
